# P12-MESH-005 gate G4 / step 20: two-dimensional bit identity of every quantity the 3D generalisation touches.
# Probe source: results/p12-mesh-005/tools/bitprobe.cpp. For each mesh it hashes (FNV-1a over the exact IEEE bits):
#   geometry  = unit normals, non-orthogonal decompositions (internal + boundary), non-orthogonality angles,
#               owner-neighbour crossings (t, point, skew vector) and skewness of every face;
#   operators = GG and LSQ gradients, diffusion (plain and non-orthogonal-corrected, both gradient schemes),
#               face interpolation, convection (upwind, central, linear_upwind, quick), the assembled energy
#               system (matrix values + rhs, non-orthogonal correction on), vector interpolation, skew-corrected
#               scalar and vector interpolation, vector error norms -- each with Dirichlet and Neumann data;
# plus the mesh fingerprint and the MeshQuality summary/issues. Meshes: two programmatic Cartesian meshes and
# the mesh of every committed case (Cartesian, graded, distorted structured_quad, multi-block).
# BASE = the pre-MESH-005 tree ($HOME/m5ref/base, Release); NEW = the final MESH-005 tree (build/release).

